course: dictionary
lesson: 14614
title: Popping: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the author means. «The popcorn was popping in the pan.» Here popping means making short, sharp bursting sounds, because the corn is bursting open.
explain: «I'm popping to the shop, back in five minutes.» Popping somewhere means going there quickly or for a short time. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «I'm going to the shop, back in five minutes» still makes sense.
explain: Popping can also mean putting something somewhere quickly, as in «Pop it in the bag.» Popping up means appearing suddenly, as in «Mice were popping up all over the field.» Read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
fact: Popping is a form of the verb pop: pop, pops, popped, popping.
fact: Popping can mean making a short, sharp bursting sound, like a balloon or popcorn.
fact: Popcorn kernels pop because the water inside turns to steam and bursts the shell.
fact: Popping can mean going somewhere quickly or for a short time, as in «popping to the shop».
fact: «Eyes popping out» shows great surprise.
exercise: «The popcorn was popping in the pan.» What does popping mean here? | *Making short, sharp bursting sounds | Staying very still | Going to the pan quickly | Putting the corn in a bag
exercise: «I'm popping to the shop, back soon.» What does popping mean? | Putting the shop in a box | Bursting like a balloon | *Going there quickly for a short time | Falling fast asleep
exercise: «Pop the sweets in the bag.» What does pop mean? | *Put quickly | Climb high | Sing softly | Burst loudly
test: «Her eyes were popping out with surprise.» What does this show about her? | *She is very surprised | She is very sleepy | She is very hungry | She is very cold
test: «Bubbles pop when their skin breaks.» What does pop mean here? | *Burst with a short, sharp sound | Float slowly up into the sky | Grow bigger and bigger | Turn into water
exam: «Mice were popping up all over the field.» What does popping up mean? | Growing very slowly | *Appearing suddenly | Singing loudly | Sinking into the ground
